/E (So, what is the chain of custody? The definition of the chain of custody is the procedure, documentation, tracking, and protecting of evidence on its journey from a crime scene to the courtroom. This documentation process protects evidence from contamination and tampering. It is also sometimes called the chain of evidence. If the chain of custody has been broken or tampered with, evidence can be ruled as inadmissible, meaning it cannot be presented or )
/Pg 16 0 R
