1955 0 obj
<<
/Title (AI algorithms are based on human-created patterns, which means that bias can exist within these algorithms, just as they do within human nature. Acknowledging the fact that AI bias can exist, particularly in areas such as facial recognition, risk assessment and criminal profiling, is  essential. AI bias can be found within the training data that the algorithm uses, the algorithm  itself or within the predictive analysis produced by the algorithm. Digital forensic scientists must work to develop and implement AI systems that are fair and unbiased to protect the integrity of their investigations and ensure that results are accurate.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
